<title>USA: Moody's cut Miami, Fla., GOs to Baa from single-A.</title>
<headline>Moody's cut Miami, Fla., GOs to Baa from single-A.</headline>
<dateline>MIAMI 1996-10-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Moody's Investors Service cut Miami's general obligation bond rating to Baa from single-A on Friday, Moody's analyst John Incorvaia told Reuters.</p>
<p>The city is struggling to close a $68 million gap in its $175 million budget for fiscal 1997, which began Oct 1.</p>
<p>&quot;Considering the magnitude of the problem in relation to the budget, we felt that it was an appropriate level,&quot; Incorvaia said.</p>
<p>A release on the downgrade is expected to be issued by the rating agency later on Friday.</p>
<p>--Jane Sutton, 305-374-5013</p>
</text>
